# 📥 **4. Load All Tables**

```python
orders = spark.read.csv("Orders.csv", header=True, inferSchema=True)
customers = spark.read.csv("Customers.csv", header=True, inferSchema=True)
products = spark.read.csv("Products.csv", header=True, inferSchema=True)
payments = spark.read.csv("Payments.csv", header=True, inferSchema=True)
returns = spark.read.csv("Returns.csv", header=True, inferSchema=True)
```

---

# 🔍 **5. Basic Exploration**

```python
orders.printSchema()
orders.describe().show()

orders.select("order_status").distinct().show()
```

---

# 🧹 **6. Data Cleaning**

## Remove Nulls

```python
orders = orders.dropna()
```

## Remove Duplicates

```python
orders = orders.dropDuplicates()
```

## Filter Invalid Data

```python
orders = orders.filter(orders.quantity > 0)
orders = orders.filter(orders.unit_price > 0)
```

---

# 🔗 **7. Data Integration (JOINS)**

## Join Orders + Customers

```python
df = orders.join(customers, "customer_id", "inner")
```

## Join Products

```python
df = df.join(products, "product_id", "inner")
```

## Join Payments

```python
df = df.join(payments, "order_id", "left")
```

## Join Returns

```python
df = df.join(returns, "order_id", "left")
```

---

# 🔄 **8. Feature Engineering**

## Total Revenue (if not present)

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import col

df = df.withColumn("revenue",
    col("quantity") * col("unit_price") * (1 - col("discount"))
)
```

---

## Profit Margin

```python
df = df.withColumn("profit_margin",
    col("profit") / col("revenue")
)
```

---

## Extract Time Features

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import to_date, month, year

df = df.withColumn("order_date", to_date("order_date"))
df = df.withColumn("month", month("order_date"))
df = df.withColumn("year", year("order_date"))
```

---

# 📊 **9. Advanced Transformations**

## 1. GroupBy Aggregation

```python
df.groupBy("category").sum("revenue").show()
```

---

## 2. Multi Aggregation

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import avg, max, min

df.groupBy("category").agg(
    avg("revenue"),
    max("revenue"),
    min("revenue")
).show()
```

---

## 3. Pivot Table

```python
df.groupBy("category").pivot("payment_method").sum("revenue").show()
```

---

## 4. Conditional Column

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import when

df = df.withColumn("order_flag",
    when(col("revenue") > 5000, "High")
    .otherwise("Low")
)
```

---

## 5. Filtering

```python
df.filter(df.order_status == "Returned").show()
```

---

# 🧠 **10. Window Functions (Advanced)**

```python
from pyspark.sql.window import Window
from pyspark.sql.functions import rank

windowSpec = Window.partitionBy("customer_id").orderBy(col("revenue").desc())

df = df.withColumn("rank", rank().over(windowSpec))
```

---

## Top Orders per Customer

```python
df.filter(df.rank == 1).show()
```

---

# 📈 **11. Business Insights Queries**

## Top Customers

```python
df.groupBy("customer_id").sum("revenue") \
  .orderBy("sum(revenue)", ascending=False).show(10)
```

---

## Monthly Sales Trend

```python
df.groupBy("year", "month").sum("revenue").show()
```

---

## Return Rate

```python
df.filter(df.return_reason.isNotNull()).count() / df.count()
```

---

## Best Selling Products

```python
df.groupBy("product_name").sum("quantity") \
  .orderBy("sum(quantity)", ascending=False).show(10)
```

